  "definition": "Risk Adjustment Mechanism",
  "effectiveDate": "2009-10-19",
  "historyNote": "#7434, INTERIM, eff 2-1-01, EXPIRED: 7-31-01 New. #7583, eff 11-1-01; ss by #9564, eff 10-19-09",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ins 3401.08",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 3401.08 Risk Adjustment Mechanism",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-07-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3401.08 Risk Adjustment Mechanism. In order to reduce the incentive for risk selection and to improve fairness and efficiency, and in the absence of a risk adjustment mechanism established by rule or order for the entire small group market, an alliance may establish a payment mechanism to adjust payments to the participating carrier or carriers prospectively or retrospectively based on the amount of risk covered by each participating carrier. To establish such a mechanism, the alliance may appoint an advisory committee composed of individuals that have risk adjustment and actuarial expertise to help establish the risk adjusters.\n\nSource. #7434, INTERIM, eff 2-1-01, EXPIRED: 7-31-01\n\nNew. #7583, eff 11-1-01; ss by #9564, eff 10-19-09",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3400.html"
